{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed (AC1) from Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744): failures show (a) `bash` output `W\\x00i\\x00n\\x00d\\x00o\\x00w\\x00s\\x00 \\x00S\\x00u\\x00b\\x00s\\x00y\\x00s\\x00t\\x00e\\x00m...` (WSL launcher, no distro, exit 1) in test_reconcile_workflow_lint, test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow, test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew; (b) `OSError: [WinError 193] %1 is not a valid Win32 application` running shebang stubs (test_child_oracle_fail_open, test_jira_pressure_test_preflight, test_reviewbot_entrypoint, test_code_review_ws5); (c) `[WinError 2]` resolving `#!/bin/sh` stubs on PATH (reclaim scripts, cast_gerrit_verified_vote, bridge_provider_wrappers).\n\nFix (commit d782dd17ea6 locally): `posix_shell_available()` + `requires_posix_shell` in tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py; per-function marks (plus per-param marks on 2 of 3 `test_an_empty_capture...` cases; module marks only for scenario4, inventory, install_sandbox_bwrap). 136 lines leave posix-shell.args, 21 leave path-separators.args. On macOS all 441 tests in the touched modules pass, zero skips carry the new reason. The 7 remaining manifest lines are removed (and both argfiles deleted) by the stacked arctic-unsecular-esok commit.\n\nWhy these are skips, not ports: each test exercises POSIX shell semantics (CI step bodies under bash, host scripts, sh command stubs) that have no Windows equivalent; Linux CI keeps running all of them."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795028632709730742,"uuid":"c1be6b0f-5ed7-4f77-bdd5-30c7adc98162"}